#!/bin/bash
# On the controller, as speedr (cron, every night): for every implementation
# that tracks a branch (`track` in impls/<name>/impl.toml), queue a run of the
# branch when its head moved: a commit not yet queued by this, nor measured.
#
#   speedr-nightly [RESULTS]   default ~/speedR-results
set -euo pipefail
repo=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
results=${1:-$HOME/speedR-results}
queued=$HOME/.speedr-nightly   # "<impl> <commit>" for every commit queued so far
touch "$queued"
speedr=$repo/.venv/bin/speedr
for name in $("$speedr" impls | awk '{ print $1 }'); do
    eval "$("$speedr" impls "$name")"
    [ -n "$impl_track" ] || continue
    commit=$(git ls-remote "$impl_repo" "refs/heads/$impl_track" | cut -f1)
    [ -n "$commit" ] || { echo "$name: no branch $impl_track in $impl_repo" >&2; continue; }
    grep -qx "$name $commit" "$queued" && continue
    if compgen -G "$results/*/$name/*/${commit:0:12}" > /dev/null; then   # measured already
        echo "$name $commit" >> "$queued"; continue
    fi
    # the job takes the branch's head when it starts, and records the branch
    echo "$(date -u +%FT%TZ) $name $impl_track at ${commit:0:12}: $(/usr/local/bin/speedr-submit run "$name@$impl_track")"
    echo "$name $commit" >> "$queued"
done
